# Line endings are decided here rather than by each clone's `core.autocrlf`.
#
# A Windows clone with `core.autocrlf=true` — the default that installer sets —
# rewrites every checked-out text file to CRLF. Two things then break, and
# neither says why. `cargo fmt --check` reports a diff on every line of every
# file, because rustfmt writes LF. And a fixture's bytes change, so the `sha256`
# a test compares an archive against is computed over a file that is no longer
# the one that was committed (§12: a file with the right name is not the same
# file). R10.8.
#
# Everything tracked here is text: source, manifests, documents, workflows,
# licences and one JSON fixture. `text=auto` still lets git decline to touch
# anything it detects as binary, so a future binary fixture is safe by default.
* text=auto eol=lf
